@C.PASS2
Syntax: C.Pass2 [<opts>] <file>
Usage : C compiler second pass - generate 6809 assembler source
Opts  :
  -o=<file>  write output to <file> (default: standard output)
  -s         strip symbol information from the output
  -p         emit profiling information
Note  : reads intermediate code from c.pass1 and writes 6809 assembler
        source for c.opt / c.asm.  Normally run by CC1, not directly.
